# T5.4 case 5 on SQL Server: F5 over a pad whose second statement the server
# says no to. `docs/DESIGN.md` ("Results grid") fixes what that does: the
# failure stops the run, so the third statement never runs; the footer says
# which one it was; the pane shows the driver's own words; and the pad paints
# that statement's lines in the error background until the next edit — which
# scripts/qa/query-workflow.sh reads out of the styles dump.

key c
wait busy
expect ●

key Tab
type select 1 as one
key Enter
key Enter
type select * from bench.nope_not_here
key Enter
key Enter
type select 3 as three
key F5
wait busy

expect statement 2 of 3 failed
expect Invalid object name
expect-not Running
frame fail-second
key Ctrl-Q
